The original has three problems. `height: auto` can't be transitioned, so the modal snaps. `top` and `all` animate layout properties, which causes jank. And `ease` at 0.3s feels generic. The fix is to animate only `opacity` and `transform` (GPU-composited), use a custom easing curve, and add a backdrop and a subtle scale.

```css
:root {
  --ease-out-expo: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);   /* fast start, long soft settle */
  --ease-in-quad:  cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.75, 0);   /* quick, decisive exit */
}

/* Backdrop */
.modal-backdrop {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  background: rgb(10 10 15 / 0.45);
  backdrop-filter: blur(0px);
  opacity: 0;
  visibility: hidden;
  transition:
    opacity 200ms var(--ease-in-quad),
    backdrop-filter 200ms var(--ease-in-quad),
    visibility 0s linear 200ms;            /* hide after fade-out finishes */
}
.modal-backdrop.open {
  opacity: 1;
  visibility: visible;
  backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
  transition:
    opacity 350ms var(--ease-out-expo),
    backdrop-filter 350ms var(--ease-out-expo),
    visibility 0s;
}

/* Modal */
.modal {
  position: fixed;
  top: 20%;                                 /* final position is static, never animated */
  left: 50%;
  translate: -50% 0;                        /* keeps centering separate from the animated transform */
  height: auto;
  opacity: 0;
  visibility: hidden;
  transform: translateY(16px) scale(0.96);
  transform-origin: 50% 0;
  will-change: transform, opacity;
  transition:
    opacity 180ms var(--ease-in-quad),
    transform 180ms var(--ease-in-quad),
    visibility 0s linear 180ms;
}
.modal.open {
  opacity: 1;
  visibility: visible;
  transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
  transition:
    opacity 300ms var(--ease-out-expo),
    transform 450ms var(--ease-out-expo),
    visibility 0s;
}

/* Optional: stagger content in after the shell lands */
.modal > * {
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translateY(8px);
  transition: opacity 250ms var(--ease-out-expo), transform 350ms var(--ease-out-expo);
}
.modal.open > * { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
.modal.open > *:nth-child(1) { transition-delay: 60ms; }
.modal.open > *:nth-child(2) { transition-delay: 110ms; }
.modal.open > *:nth-child(3) { transition-delay: 160ms; }

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .modal, .modal.open, .modal > *, .modal-backdrop, .modal-backdrop.open {
    transform: none;
    transition-duration: 1ms;
    transition-delay: 0s;
  }
}
```

**Why this feels premium**
- **Only compositor properties animate.** `opacity` and `transform` run at 60fps and avoid the layout thrash from animating `top` or `height`. Use the individual `translate` property for centering so it doesn't collide with the animated `transform`.
- **Custom easing.** The expo-out curve starts fast and settles gently, which reads as physical. `ease` is the default everyone recognizes as generic.
- **Asymmetric timing.** Entering takes about 300–450ms. Leaving takes about 180ms with ease-in. Users want dismissal to feel snappy.
- **Small scale (0.96) plus an 8–16px rise.** Subtle depth without a "bouncy" cartoon feel. Anchoring the origin at the top matches where the modal sits.
- **Backdrop blur and fade.** This separates the layers and focuses attention.
- **`visibility` with a delayed transition.** The modal stays out of the tab order and pointer events once closed, but still fades out fully.
- **Staggered content.** A 50ms cascade makes the modal feel assembled rather than dropped in.
- **Reduced motion.** Respects `prefers-reduced-motion`.

If the modal's height needs to animate as content changes, use `grid-template-rows: 0fr → 1fr` on a wrapper, or `interpolate-size: allow-keywords` where supported. Don't animate `height: auto`.

If you want a slight overshoot, swap the enter easing for `cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.4, 0.64, 1)` on `transform` only. Keep it on transform and not opacity.

